A||||5||REDHOTT88||Synthetic oil and additives do they mix?||||5||
Z||000000||REDHOTT88||12-13-2001||06:27 PM||||I've been running Mobil 1 for a while now in all my vehicles, including my beloved Fiero.<P>Anyone know if STP oil treatment, Restore or any of those other additives will mix with synthetics? Or should I stay away.  I know everyone will have an opnion so lets hear em!<P>I have an 88 truck that used conventional oil, burned a little oil (blue smoke at first start up) but seemed to run quieter and smoother, with no smoke, when Restore was put in it a couple years ago..  I switched to Mobil 1 this year.<P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over, runs smooth, shifts crisp!)</FONT>||||reg||5
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-13-2001||08:00 PM||||Do you hear crickets? I hear crickets..<P>Boy, this is a lonely topic.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||12-13-2001||08:22 PM||||Please send me all the money you want to spend on oil additives.  Most additives are a waste of money, and yes, most all oils will mix with other oils.  STP is just a heavy weight oil.<P>Mobil 1 is just fine by its expensive self.||||reg||1
Z||000003||jelly2m8||12-13-2001||08:25 PM||||NO! NEVER mix any additives with any synthetic oils.<P> For example, Slick50 and Valvoline mixed makes oil with the consistancy of cold molasses.<P>  A few years ago the local canadian tire store mixed synthetic oils with additives, and several people had seized engines within 60 miles.<P> Alot of people got fired over that, as they had to go good for these engines.<BR>Needless to say, they didn't mix synthetic oil with anything after that.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||12-13-2001||08:31 PM||||SKIP the addatives.  They're junk, all of them.  Go with a good weighty synthetic (mobil 1 15-w50 is good in older oil-burners, in temprate climates only)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||REDHOTT88||12-13-2001||08:42 PM||||Alright, the NAY's are outweighing the YA's.<P>I think I got my answer!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"><P>Thank you||||reg||1
